  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`: `@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())` now parses `key=value` strings into a `(key, value)` tuple. The existing test suite still passes, but I didn't add tests for `KeyValue` itself.\n\nI checked these inputs with `CliRunner`:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `a=b` | `('a', 'b')` |\n| `a=b=c` | `('a', 'b=c')` (splits at the first `=`) |\n| `a=` | `('a', '')` (empty value allowed) |\n| `novalue` | exit 2, `'novalue' is not a valid key=value pair.` |\n| `=x` | exit 2, `'=x' is not a valid key=value pair.` |\n\nThe class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n\nAn empty value like `a=` is accepted because you only asked for no `=` or an empty key to fail. If you want an empty value rejected as well, it's a one-line change.",
